# Sokka's Haiku counters a noncreature spell (Black Lotus), then draws, then mills three, then untaps Bot1's own tapped
# Island, in that order (CR 608.2c). Bot1's library holds exactly two cards: draw first leaves one card to mill, so the
# milling is cut short at one card and nobody has lost; milled first and then drawn, the empty library would be drawn from
# and Bot1 would lose. The spell is Bot2's Black Lotus, so it is never on the battlefield. "Target spell" refuses the
# Haiku itself (CR 115.5) and a permanent (the Island, which the land target then takes).

[Bot1 Deck]
Sokka's Haiku
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island
Island
Island
Plains
Swamp

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {U}{U}{U}{U}{B}
Bot1.Hand.Sokka's Haiku.Cast
! Bot1.Target(Stack.Sokka's Haiku)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Target(Stack.Black Lotus)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Island)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Black Lotus
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
